      "message": "There still some behaviour difference between ashmem and memfd without F_SEAL_SEAL.\n\nIIRC on the kernel source code, if F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE is set without F_SEAL_SEAL. An untrusted process would still be able to set F_SEAL_WRITE and cause crash on the other process when it writes on previously mapped shared memory region. Potentially introduce a bug that can cause DDoS.",
