      "side": 1,
      "message": "The kernel keeps track of shared mappings that are writable or may become writable in the future, and prevents `F_SEAL_WRITE` from being applied if there are any such mappings.\n\nIIUC, in the scenario that you described, there must exist a writable mapping at the time which `F_SEAL_WRITE` is applied, and the process that would access that would use that mapping to write would encounter an error. However, this situation cannot arise, as `F_SEAL_WRITE` would not be applied successfully, so I don\u0027t see how this could be a threat model.",
